  "generated_text": "To determine the units digit of the sum \\(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \\ldots + 3^{2009}\\), we first need to identify the units digits of the individual terms in the sequence. We start by examining the pattern in the units digits of the powers of 3.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^1 & = 3 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 3)} \\\\\n3^2 & = 9 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 9)} \\\\\n3^3 & = 27 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 7)} \\\\\n3^4 & = 81 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 1)} \\\\\n3^5 & = 243 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 3)} \\\\\n3^6 & = 729 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 9)} \\\\\n3^7 & = 2187 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 7)} \\\\\n3^8 & = 6561 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 1)} \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nWe observe that the units digits repeat every 4 terms: 3, 9, 7, 1. Therefore, the units digits of the terms \\(3^1, 3^3, 3^5, \\ldots, 3^{2009}\\) form a repeating sequence of 3, 7, 3, 1. \n\nNext, we count the number of terms in the sequence \\(3^1, 3^3, 3^5, \\ldots, 3^{2009}\\). This is an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common difference \\(d = 2\\). The \\(n\\)-th term of this sequence is given by:\n\n\\[\na_n = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 2 = 2n - 1\n\\]\n\nSetting \\(a_n = 2009\\), we solve for \\(n\\):\n\n\\[\n2n - 1 = 2009 \\implies 2n = 2010 \\implies n = 1005\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 1005 terms in the sequence. Since the units digits repeat every 4 terms, we divide 1005 by 4 to find the number of complete cycles and the remaining terms:\n\n\\[\n1005 \\div 4 = 251 \\text{ remainder } 1\n\\]\n\nThis means there are 251 complete cycles of 3, 7, 3, 1 and 1 additional term (which is 3).\n\nNow, we calculate the sum of the units digits in one complete cycle (3, 7, 3, 1):\n\n\\[\n3 + 7 + 3 + 1 = 14\n\\]\n\nSince there are 251 complete cycles, the sum of the units digits of these cycles is:\n\n\\[\n251 \\times 14 = 3514\n\\]\n\nThe units digit of 3514 is 4. Adding the units digit of the remaining term (3):\n\n\\[\n4 + 3 = 7\n\\]\n\nThus, the units digit of the sum \\(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \\ldots + 3^{2009}\\) is \\(\\boxed{7}\\).",
